# AI DIRECTIVE: TDD WORKFLOW
⚠️ CRITICAL TESTING DIRECTIVE ⚠️

You must follow these steps in order for each feature:

1. Write Failing Test
   - Create test file if needed
   - Write simplest possible test
   - Ensure test fails
   - Document in active-working-feature-context.mdc
   - Update feature status to [test-failing]

2. Implement Minimum Code
   - Write simplest code to pass test
   - Follow SOLID principles
   - Document implementation
   - Update feature status to [implementing]

3. Run Tests
   - Execute all tests
   - Verify new test passes
   - Ensure no regressions
   - Document results
   - Update feature status to [test-passing]

4. Refactor
   - Clean up code
   - Remove duplication
   - Improve readability
   - Run tests again
   - Update feature status to [refactored]

5. Performance Check
   - Run performance metrics
   - Verify no degradation
   - Document results
   - Update feature status to [performance-verified]

6. Update Context
   - Update active-working-feature-context.mdc
   - Document progress
   - Note any issues
   - Plan next test

7. Repeat
   - Write next failing test
   - Continue cycle
   - Until feature is complete

Status Tracking:
- [test-failing]: Test written but failing
- [implementing]: Writing code to pass test
- [test-passing]: Test passing
- [refactored]: Code cleaned up
- [performance-verified]: Performance checked
- [complete]: All tests passing, code clean, performance verified

---

After completing TDD cycle:
1. Update active-working-feature-context.mdc
2. Follow performance-check.mdc
3. Proceed to next test or feature 